  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Get-or-compute hot-path optimizations on top of 2.3.0 stampede protection: GetString and GetOrComputeString decode straight off the native buffer (no intermediate byte[]); a new zero-allocation GetOrCompute(byte[] key, Span<byte> destination, factory, out written) overload copies into the caller buffer on a hit; the single-flight miss path avoids per-call closures. API change: GetOrComputeAsync now returns ValueTask<byte[]> (was Task<byte[]>) so a hit allocates no Task — source-compatible for `await` callers.",
